<title>USA: U.S. mediator to talk with UPS, Teamsters.</title>
<headline>U.S. mediator to talk with UPS, Teamsters.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>John Wells, the federal mediator in talks between United Parcel Service and the Teamsters union, said on Tuesday he planned to speak with both parties in an attempt to halt the two-day-old strike.</p>
<p>&quot;I am going to be in touch with both sides this morning as I was yesterday morning and yesterday afternoon and we'll just have to see where it goes,&quot; he told the Cable News Network.</p>
<p>When asked if there were any negotiations scheduled for Tuesday, Wells said: &quot;Not that I'm aware of.&quot;</p>
<p>But he added: &quot;I am hopeful that both parties will be willing to get a negotiated settlement in the near future.&quot;</p>
</text>
